\description{
Dense sampling (e.g. the Alps, Scandinavia) puts many records into the same
part of environmental space, so models overweight those conditions.
\code{thin_environment()} keeps a set of records that represents the environment
of \emph{all} records, without an arbitrary target number, and without
truncating the niche environmentally or geographically:
}
\details{
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Environmental space.} A PCA is fitted on a random sample of the whole
raster area (the environment available to the species, e.g. M) and the
records are placed in it; the first PCs explaining at least
\code{pc_cumvar} of the variance are used (\code{axes = "raw"} uses the
standardised layers instead). Precipitation amounts (\code{log_vars}) are
log-transformed for this space only, so that differences count in
relative terms.
\item \strong{Bin width from the data.} Every record is accurate to \code{radius_km},
so its true position may be any cell within that distance of its cell
(the window spans more columns at high latitudes, where cells are
narrow). The range of each axis within the window is the record's
\emph{environmental uncertainty}; the bin width of each axis is its median
(\code{width_quantile}) over all records. Two records in one bin differ less
than a single record's own uncertainty: they are environmental
duplicates.
\item \strong{One record per bin} (\code{max_per_bin}), the one closest to the bin's
centre (\code{pick = "central"}) or a random one. Every occupied bin keeps a
record, so every removed record has a kept one less than one bin width
away on every axis: only the density is evened out.
\item \strong{Always kept:} records you protect (e.g. genetic samples), the minimum
and maximum of every layer (optionally the outer tails), and the convex
hull vertices of every pair of axes (extreme \emph{combinations} of
conditions).
\item \strong{Geographic quota:} the area is cut into \code{block_km} equal-area blocks
and every block keeps at least \verb{min(block_min, records it had)};
missing records are added choosing the least represented environments
first. Small or isolated areas and lone records are kept.
}

